      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T23:45:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, the idea is that `TEXT_MAP_ITEM` is indeed always undefined. Every usage of `EC_STATUS_TEXT` must define `TEXT_MAP_ITEM` before and then undef immediately after.\n\nIn this case we used it above in `BUILD_ASSERT`, which was fully evaluated. Honestly, I was surprised that we didn\u0027t need to define `TEXT_MAP_ITEM` before defining `EC_STATUS_TEXT` (or before including this file in other source files). I guess CPP can do multiple rounds of substitution.",
